---
title: Privacy
---

This site counts page requests. It measures how you read a post only if you
press the line that asks.

## What is recorded

Cloudflare hosts this site. When your browser asks for a page, a small
program at Cloudflare counts the request and sends a record of it to my
collector. Nothing runs on your device for this. The record holds what your
browser sends with any page request, and what Cloudflare looks up from your
connection:

- the page you opened, and the campaign parameters in the link
  (`utm_source` and the like) if it had any
- the page you came from, if your browser says
- your browser's user-agent string, and the browser version, operating system
  and phone flag that some browsers send with every request
- the headers that say what kind of request it was, such as whether you
  followed a link from another site
- the country, the network's number and the Cloudflare data centre your
  connection comes through, as Cloudflare reports them. I keep the number
  only, never the network's name, so the data cannot say which company or
  school you read from

The headers and the network number help me tell people from bots. Images, scripts
and other files are not counted. A page your browser fetches ahead of a
click, for example while the pointer rests on its link, is recorded and
marked as fetched ahead. It counts as a view even if you never open it. If
you open it within five minutes, it counts once.

## How visitors are counted without identifying anyone

Counting unique readers normally requires tagging the device. Instead, the
server combines your IP address, your browser's user agent and a secret that
changes every day, and keeps only the resulting hash. Your IP address is
discarded immediately and never written down. The daily secret is deleted
after three days, and once it is gone the stored hashes cannot be traced back
to anyone, including by me. I cannot tell whether you visited on an earlier
day, on this device or any other.

## Reading, only if you ask

Each post has one line under its title: "Help me improve this post: share how
you read it." A small script draws that line. Until you press it, the script
sends nothing.

Pressing it starts a reading script for that page only. It runs while the
page is open, until you press Stop. The next post asks again. While it runs, it
records:

- how long you read actively, meaning the tab is visible and in focus and you
  scrolled, tapped, typed or moved the pointer in the last five seconds
- how long the page was visible but not in focus
- for each part of the post, how long it was on screen while you read, and
  when and how often it came into view
- the furthest part you reached, where you were last, and whether you reached
  the end
- how often you used the interactive demos, and how long one was on screen
  while you read
- the links you followed: whether each led to another page here, a reference
  or another site, which site, and where in the post the link was
- the page you came from

It also sends the post's outline (its parts, their headings and word counts),
which says nothing about you. It does not record what you type or where the
pointer is. It sends what it has every 15 seconds and when you hide or leave
the page. Each report reaches my collector with your user-agent string and
your IP address, which are handled as described above.

## Why there is no consent banner

The count happens at Cloudflare, on the request your browser sends for any
page, and runs nothing on your device. The reading script does run in your
browser, so it waits until you press the line on a post, and it covers that
post only. The site asks there instead of with a banner on every page.

## Legal basis

The count rests on my legitimate interest in knowing how the site is used
(GDPR Art. 6(1)(f)). You can object to it by writing to the address below.
The reading measurement rests on your consent, which you give by pressing the
line on a post (Art. 6(1)(a)).

## What is stored on your device

Nothing, unless you ask for the one cookie that turns counting off (below).
No local storage. No session storage.

## If you have Global Privacy Control turned on

Your page requests are not counted: the counter at Cloudflare sees the
signal and sends nothing.
Posts do not show the line that asks, and the reading script does not start.

## Turning counting off for one browser

Open
[andreasbogossian.com/_readlog/ignore](https://andreasbogossian.com/_readlog/ignore)
in a browser to stop counting it. That sets one cookie, `rl_ignore`, which
says only "do not count" and lasts about 400 days. Open
[andreasbogossian.com/_readlog/count](https://andreasbogossian.com/_readlog/count)
to remove it.

## Who sees this

Cloudflare processes your page requests and carries the reports to my
collector, on my behalf. Apart from that, nobody sees the data but me. It sits
on a machine in my home, not with an analytics company. It is not sold, shared or fed to anything.

## How long it is kept

Records of visits and reads are deleted after 25 months.

## Questions and complaints

Write to [contact@andreasbogossian.com](mailto:contact@andreasbogossian.com)
with any question, or to object to any of this. You also have the right to
complain to the Finnish Data Protection Ombudsman at
[tietosuoja.fi/en](https://tietosuoja.fi/en).
